# Keeps the build context small and host-only files out of the image.

.git

# `.env` alone does not match `.env.local`, and that distinction matters here: Vite loads
# `.env.local` in *every* mode, production builds included. The checked-out file sets
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001 and VITE_ENABLE_MOCKS=true, so leaving it in the
# context would put a developer's localhost origin inside the build.
#
# (Real process environment variables outrank .env files in Vite, so the Dockerfile's ARG
# would have won anyway, and MSW is gated on `import.meta.env.DEV` regardless. This is the
# belt to that braces -- the failure mode is a bundle that silently points at the wrong host,
# which is exactly the class of bug the same-origin setup exists to prevent.)
.env
.env.*

node_modules

# Rebuilt inside the image by `npm run build`. A stale host copy would be copied in and then
# overwritten, or worse, partially shadow the fresh one.
dist
dist-ssr
.vite

coverage
*.log

data
